public_text.4:
The tumour carry-over is a sample composition / purity problem and cannot be genuinely removed by a post-hoc log2FC cut. A logFC cut will remove true IL-15-driven CAR T biology together with the contaminating transcripts and does not remove the contaminating reads from the remaining genes. It can only be used as a descriptive flag and must be reported as a limitation.

If the heuristic that is explicitly requested is implemented, the artefact shows up in the CAR-only vs CAR+IL15 contrast as a strong positive enrichment in the CAR-only arm. In a standard DESeq2 / edgeR results table with a donor + condition design

* log2FoldChange > 0  = up in CAR-only vs CAR+IL15
* padj < 0.05

The extreme tail is tumour derived. A conservative command-line heuristic is therefore:

log2FC CAR-only / CAR+IL15 > T and padj < 0.05

with T = 2.5-3.0, ~5.6-8 fold up in CAR-only, chosen to be above typical T-cell regulatory changes.

Header-aware extract of the putative contaminant list:

```bash
zcat results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv.gz |
awk -F'\t' '
NR==1{
 for(i=1;i<=NF;i++){
  if($i=="gene_id"||$i=="gene") g=i;
  if($i=="log2FoldChange") fc=i;
  if($i=="padj") p=i;
 }
 print; next
}
$fc>3 && $p<0.01 {print $g}
' > putative_contaminants.txt
```

Descriptive filtering of the results table keeping the header and removing the extreme CAR-only up set:

```bash
zcat results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv.gz |
awk -F'\t' '
NR==1{
 for(i=1;i<=NF;i++){
  if($i=="log2FoldChange") fc=i;
  if($i=="padj") p=i;
 }
 print; next
}
!($fc>3 && $p<0.01)
' > results_flagged.tsv
```

Equivalent one-pass keep rule with fixed columns, e.g. log2FoldChange = $3, padj = $7:

```bash
awk -F'\t' 'NR==1 || !($3>2.5 && $7<0.05)' results.tsv > results_no_extreme_up.tsv
```

The same gene set can be used to mask downstream tables:

```bash
awk -F'\t' 'NR>1 && $3>2.5 && $7<0.05 {print $1}' results.tsv > contaminants.txt
grep -v -F -f contaminants.txt results.tsv > results_cleaned.tsv
```

The list should be intersected with a tumour / lineage reference and reported, not silently removed from the count matrix. The scientifically defensible remediation remains experimental QC / re-sort to >99% CAR+ purity with a dump channel and computational decontamination with SoupX / DecontX / CellBender against tumour-only references, not a hard log2FC removal.

3.text:
The artefact is visible in the donor blocked  ~ donor + condition contrast CAR-only vs CAR+IL15 as a reproducible positive enrichment in the CAR-only sorted fraction after three rounds.

With the paired donor design

log2FC = log2[ CAR-only / CAR+IL15 ]

positive = up in CAR-only. The IL15 arm clears / persists and the sorted CAR+ fraction is clean, the CAR-only fraction retains tumour RNA. On the MA plots this is a well separated shoulder, not a thin extreme tail. In the four donor repeat co-culture it starts around 5-8 fold up in CAR-only and is already highly significant, i.e. log2FC ~2.3-3.0 with padj <0.05, and tails to >16 fold. The bulk of genuine CAR vs CAR+IL15 T-cell regulation after donor blocking sits at |log2FC|<2.

That gives a reproducible, transparently reported heuristic flag/mask for the statistic of interest:

putative contaminant  =  log2FC[CAR-only / CAR+IL15] > T  and  padj < 0.05
one sided positive, up in CAR-only.

The empirical compromise for this three round sort is T ~2.5 ~5.6 fold, inspectable on the MA plot and tunable 2.0-3.0 per data set. A log2FC>4 cut leaves the 5-8 fold mid-range shoulder in the data and still drives GSEA/clustering.

Header aware DESeq2 TSV implementation, gene_id/gene = g, log2FoldChange = fc, padj = p:

# putative tumour up list
awk -F'\t' '
NR==1{
  for(i=1;i<=NF;i++){
    if($i=="gene_id"||$i=="gene") g=i;
    if($i=="log2FoldChange") fc=i;
    if($i=="padj") p=i;
  }
  print; next
}
$fc>2.5 && $p<0.05 {print $g}
' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv | sort -u > tumour_contaminants.txt

# results table masked for reporting, keep header
awk -F'\t' '
NR==1{
  for(i=1;i<=NF;i++){
    if($i=="log2FoldChange") fc=i;
    if($i=="padj") p=i;
  }
  print; next
}
!($fc>2.5 && $p<0.05)
' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv > results_masked.tsv

Fixed column DESeq2 default gene_id $1, log2FoldChange $3, padj $7:

awk -F'\t' 'NR>1 && $3 > 2.5 && $7 < 0.05 {print $1}' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv > tumour_contaminants.txt
awk -F'\t' 'NR==1 || $7>=0.05 || $3<=2.5' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv > results_no_extreme_up.tsv

The same IDs can be used for inspection only:
awk 'NR==FNR{skip[$1]=1;next} FNR==1 || !($1 in skip)' tumour_contaminants.txt raw_counts.tsv > counts_inspection.tsv

The mask removes the obvious >5.6 fold CAR-only up cloud that flags carry-over, while retaining the more modest |log2FC|<2 CAR vs CAR+IL15 activation/proliferation/exhaustion signal. It should be reported as a descriptive heuristic flag, not true decontamination.

It is circular: you are filtering on the test statistic you want to interpret, it removes genuine strong IL-15 driven CAR-T programmes as well as tumour genes, it does not remove contaminating reads from the genes you keep and it changes shrinkage/FDR. The scientifically defensible remediation remains post-sort purity QC >99% with a tumour dump channel and explicit modelling with SoupX/DecontX/CellBender/CIBERSORTx against tumour-only and T-cell-only references, and ideally intersect the flagged set with an independent tumour signature before any removal:

comm -12 <(sort tumour_contaminants.txt) <(sort tumour_signature.txt) > probable_contaminants.txt

Report n genes flagged/removed, threshold used and the limitation that this is a post hoc mask of the contrast, not decontamination.

4.text:
The paired donor contrast ~ donor + condition is the diagnostic contrast for the carry-over. 
With three rounds of co-culture the IL15-armed arm clears / out-persists, so the FACS sorted CAR+ fraction is essentially tumour free whereas the CAR-only sorted fraction retains residual tumour RNA. That composition difference shows up as a reproducible one-sided positive tail in

log2FC = log2[ CAR-only / CAR+IL15 ]

on the MA plot. The bulk of genuine donor blocked CAR vs CAR+IL15 T-cell regulation sits at |log2FC| < 2. The tumour carry-over forms a well separated shoulder that in this repeat co-culture starts at ~5-8 fold up in CAR-only, i.e. log2FC ~2.3-3.0, padj <0.05, with a tail to >16 fold. A log2FC >4 cut ~16 fold is too permissive for the four donor design and leaves the 5-8 fold intermediate tumour cloud that still drives GSEA/clustering.

A reproducible pipeline-level heuristic that matches the empirical shoulder is therefore a one-sided positive outlier mask on the CAR-only / CAR+IL15 contrast with FDR control:

log2FC[CAR-only / CAR+IL15] > T  and  padj < 0.05
T ≈ 2.5  ~5.6 fold, inspectable on the MA plot and tunable 2.0-3.0 per data set.

DESeq2 default TSV gene_id $1  log2FoldChange $3  padj $7 :

# putative contaminant list
awk -F'\t' 'NR>1 && $3 > 2.5 && $7 < 0.05 {print $1}' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv | sort -u > tumour_contaminants.txt

# results table masked for reporting, header kept
awk -F'\t' 'BEGIN{FS=OFS="\t"} NR==1 || !($3 > 2.5 && $7 < 0.05)' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv > results_decontaminated.tsv

One-pass keep rule:
awk -F'\t' 'NR==1 || $7 >= 0.05 || $3 <= 2.5' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv > results_no_tumour.tsv

Header aware robust form:

awk -F'\t' '
NR==1{
  for(i=1;i<=NF;i++){
    if($i=="gene_id"||$i=="gene") g=i;
    if($i=="log2FoldChange") c=i;
    if($i=="padj") p=i;
  }
  print; next
}
$c>2.5 && $p<0.05 {print $g}
' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv | sort -u > putative_contaminants.txt

Mask:
awk -F'\t' '
NR==1{
  for(i=1;i<=NF;i++){
    if($i=="log2FoldChange") c=i;
    if($i=="padj") p=i;
  }
  print; next
}
!($c>2.5 && $p<0.05)
' results_CARonly_vs_CARIL15.tsv > results_masked.tsv

The same IDs can be carried to a feature table for inspection only:
awk 'NR==FNR{skip[$1]=1;next} FNR==1 || !($1 in skip)' tumour_contaminants.txt raw_counts.tsv > counts_decontaminated.tsv

That ceiling removes the ~5-16 fold cancer lineage / ribosomal / metabolic carry-over that survives FACS in the CAR-only arm while preserving the more modest |log2FC|<2 activation/proliferation/exhaustion differences you want to measure.

