The donor-matched CAR-only vs CAR+IL15 ~ donor + condition contrast is the diagnostic we have to use after three rounds. The IL15 arm clears / persists so the sorted CAR+ fraction is essentially tumour free, whereas the CAR-only sorted CAR+ fraction retains residual tumour RNA. That shows up as a reproducible one-sided positive enrichment in CAR-only / CAR+IL15.

Across the four donors the MA plots are consistent: the bulk of genuine donor-blocked CAR vs CAR+IL15 T-cell state changes – activation, proliferation, exhaustion – sit at |log2FC|<2. The tumour carry-over is a separate positive shoulder, not an extreme >16-fold tail only. It starts ~5-8 fold up in CAR-only, log2FC CAR-only / CAR+IL15 ~2.3-3.0, padj <0.05, with tumour lineage / ribosomal / metabolic genes that survive FACS when killing fails, and it tails to higher values.

That is why a log2FC >4 ~16-fold cut is too permissive for this design. It leaves the 5-8 fold, log2FC ~2.5-3.5, intermediate contamination in the CAR-only arm and that mid-range signal is still enough to drive GSEA, clustering and pathway scores in the CAR vs CAR+IL15 comparison.

A transparent pipeline heuristic that matches the empirical shoulder is a one-sided positive outlier mask on that contrast with FDR control:

log2FC[CAR-only / CAR+IL15] > 2.5  and  padj < 0.05

~5.6-fold up in CAR-only, inspectable on the MA plot and tunable 2.0-3.0 per dataset.

